    "id": 3932,
    "user": "Anita Wong",
    "role": "student",
    "text": "combining testing framework and AI comes for me a bit out of the blue. If you want to introduce AI to the testing framework too, you should've mentioned it earlier to avoid confusion. If you do not plan introducing AI in the testing framework, omit this sentence to avoid confusion OR highlight only the thing that testing frameworks is going to be deterministic.\nAnother point: define \"deterministic\" in this case to avoid open-end thoughts and to remain on your course of thought.",
    "annotationId": 3866,
    "parentCommendId": null,
    "tags": [],
    "votes": [
